<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia's Minas allocations raised in Feb. [CORRECTED 10:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>Indonesia's Minas allocations raised in Feb. [CORRECTED 10:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia has raised its export allocation of Minas crude oil to 90,600 barrels per day (bpd) for February (corrects from cut to 19,600) from 72,000 bpd in January, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The overall allocation was estimated at about 290,600 bpd (corrects from 220,000 bpd) from 225,000 bpd in January.</p>
<p>The following allocations of key grades were made, industry sources said (in barrels per day):</p>
<p>		   FEB	   JAN</p>
<p> MINAS	  90,600	72,000</p>
<p> DURI	   46,000	35,000</p>
<p> CINTA	  19,600	20,000</p>
<p> WIDURI	 20,400	11,000</p>
<p> ARUN	   24,000	19,000</p>
<p> BELIDA	 32,100	12,000</p>
<p> BONTANG MIX  32,900	32,000</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
